  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "BNSF Railway (Petitioner)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "86c8545503432c2bb2f43fc8fe373ae3723e99d4b40cc1a68924adba0a1434ce",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-86c854550343-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to BNSF Railway (Petitioner), according to BNSF Railway (Petitioner), bNSF Railway argues that the Montana Supreme Court\u2019s finding of general personal jurisdiction over BNSF is incorrect because the court relied on systematic and continuous business activity and on Section 56 of the Federal Employers' Liability Act."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Murray",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "86c8545503432c2bb2f43fc8fe373ae3723e99d4b40cc1a68924adba0a1434ce",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-86c854550343-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. Murray, bNSF points out that it earns up to ten percent of its total revenue in Montana, a share that is disproportionately large compared with its operations in other states."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "BNSF",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "86c8545503432c2bb2f43fc8fe373ae3723e99d4b40cc1a68924adba0a1434ce",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-86c854550343-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to BNSF, bNSF relies on the Pope and Boyd cases, which the Supreme Court has used to hold that a railroad\u2019s business activities in a state can create jurisdiction for suits arising elsewhere."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
